  "singleton_class_limitation": "PA (n=1) and PVC (n=1) each have exactly one example in the full n=14 set. In true LOOCV, when a singleton class's only example is held out, the training set contains zero examples of that class -- the model cannot have learned that class's visual signature and structurally cannot predict it correctly on that fold, regardless of model quality. This is a fundamental small-n limitation, not a bug. The full n=14 LOOCV figure includes these 2 folds (which fail by construction); the PE/PP/PS-only n=12 LOOCV figure excludes them and is the more interpretable accuracy estimate."
